Most of assets/target_data/ is redistributed from NVIDIA Proteina-Complexa
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Public License
(licenses/license_datasets.txt,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode).

    Creator:  NVIDIA Corporation
    Source:   https://github.com/NVIDIA-Digital-Bio/Proteina-Complexa
    License:  CC BY 4.0
    Modified: these are benchmark target structures that NVIDIA cropped,
              repacked or otherwise modified from their Protein Data Bank
              originals. The Prompteina authors redistribute the individual
              files unchanged, but ship a subset: the AME input structures and
              the ligand targets are omitted because this release does not
              support those tasks, and the upstream dataset ID manifests
              formerly under assets/data/ are omitted because nothing in this
              repository reads them. All of it remains available from the
              upstream repository.
    Warranty: Unless otherwise separately undertaken by the Licensor, to the
              extent possible, the Licensor offers the Licensed Material as-is
              and as-available, and makes no representations or warranties of
              any kind concerning the Licensed Material.

assets/target_data/campaign_targets/GM2A_antigen.pdb is not from upstream. The
Prompteina authors prepared it for the prospective design campaign reported in
the paper from the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database prediction for UniProt
P17900. They converted the prediction to PDB format and retained mature-chain
residues 32--193.

    Creator:    Google DeepMind
    Distributor: EMBL's European Bioinformatics Institute (EMBL-EBI)
    Source:     https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/entry/P17900
    Copyright:  AlphaFold Data Copyright (2022) DeepMind Technologies Limited
    License:    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
                https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Modified:   converted to PDB format and cropped to residues 32--193 by the
                Prompteina authors

The file carries this attribution in its PDB remarks, and
configs/targets/campaign_targets_dict.yaml records its provenance. The
AlphaFold Protein Structure Database asks users to credit EMBL-EBI and cite
Jumper et al., Nature (2021), and the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database.

The underlying records come from the Protein Data Bank, the AlphaFold Protein
Structure Database and TED, each of which carries its own upstream terms that
this grant does not override.


